// src/ctl_hci.nv — the Controller's HCI layer: the Commands it
// answers, the events it sends, and the state those commands set.
//
// The Controller is one value, `Controller`, with inline storage: the H4
// reader of `h4_rx.nv`, the packet pool of `ctl_pool.nv`, the event masks,
// the device addresses and the Filter Accept List.  A program holds it in a
// module-level `var` and drives it with four calls, in a loop:
//
//   ctl_accepts / ctl_rx    give it the octets the Host sent
//   ctl_step                answer the Command that is complete
//   ctl_tx_pending / ctl_tx_next    take the octets to send to the Host
//   ctl_async_*             finish a command that needs the hardware
//
// A Command is answered whole before the next is read: while one waits, or
// waits for the hardware, `ctl_accepts` is false and the transport holds the
// octets back with its flow control.  That keeps one Command outstanding, the
// Num_HCI_Command_Packets of 1 every answer carries ([Vol 4] Part E, Section
// 4.4), and it sizes every buffer.
//
// What the Controller answers is what `command_bit` lists, and the
// Supported_Commands bit field is built from that list, so a command is
// either answered or answered with Unknown HCI Command (0x01), and the field
// says which.  A build without a Link Layer (`CAP_LL` absent) reports no state
// and answers no command that needs one.  The Filter Accept List commands manage
// the list the advertising and scanning filter policies read.
//
// The connections.  The Link Layer holds up to `noble_controller_config.CTL_LINKS` connections
// (`ll_link.nv`), in `links`, and at most `noble_controller_config.CTL_PERIPHERAL` of them as Peripheral and
// `noble_controller_config.CTL_CENTRAL` as Central; the three are keys of the package configuration (`ctl_links`,
// `ctl_peripheral` and `ctl_central` in novo.toml).  A link's handle is its slot
// plus one.  The calls that name a link take its slot and write `c.links[slot]`, which
// is the link's own storage inside the Controller: nothing is copied.  A function that
// takes the Controller and also a link cannot be given `c` and `c.links[slot]` in one
// call (SPEC section 14.8), so it takes the slot.
//
// ACL Data from the Host goes to the queue of the link its handle names
// (`ctl_rx`), data from the peer goes to the Host as ACL Data packets
// (`ctl_conn_rx_slow`), and the events the connections owe the Host are queued as
// slots are free (`ctl_flush_events`, which `ctl_step` runs first).  The
// Initiating state (`ll_init.nv`) is entered by LE Create Connection and left when
// its CONNECT_IND is on air, which opens the Central link.
//
// No function here allocates.

